# Copy to .env for local dev (dotenv is loaded by src/config.ts).
# On Cloud Run, set these as service env vars / secrets instead of a file.

# --- Server ---
PORT=8080
# Origin allowed to call this API without a Firebase Hosting rewrite in
# front of it (local `ng serve` by default). Not needed once the
# production Angular app reaches this API through a same-origin Hosting
# rewrite — see README.md "Backend contract".
ALLOWED_ORIGIN=http://localhost:4200

# --- Auth (README.md "Backend contract": "reject any uid but yours") ---
# The Firebase Authentication uid of the single account allowed to use
# this instance. Find it in Firebase console → Authentication → Users,
# after creating your account from the Auth screen.
OWNER_UID=mhbBKFrmM3N89i1YBIYEHKcoXME2

# --- Firebase Admin credentials ---
# Local dev: path to a service account JSON key
# (Firebase console → Project settings → Service accounts → Generate new
# private key). On Cloud Run: leave unset — the attached service
# account's ambient credentials are used automatically.
GOOGLE_APPLICATION_CREDENTIALS=service-account.json

# --- allanime / ani-cli upstream ---
# ani-cli scrapes this API (see src/lib/allanime-client.ts). Its domain
# is known to rotate — these are ani-cli's current values as of this
# writing (pystardust/ani-cli, "ani-cli" script). If /api/search starts
# failing outright, diff these against the live script before assuming
# anything else is broken.
ALLANIME_API_BASE=https://api.mkissa.net
# 2026-09-11: mkissa.to itself is currently sitting behind a Cloudflare
# bot-verification wall (confirmed via community reports — see
# https://github.com/yuzono/anime-extensions/issues/607 — and reproduced
# here: /api/sources's key-derivation step was getting served a challenge
# page instead of the real homepage). allmanga.to is the newer front-end
# domain community scrapers have moved to and loads normally as of this
# writing. Only overriding the referer, not ALLANIME_API_BASE above —
# search/episodes are working fine against api.mkissa.net right now, and
# there's no confirmation the two domains share the same key material, so
# swapping the GraphQL host too risks breaking what already works. If
# /api/sources still fails after this change, check the new
# `[allanime-crypto]` log line: same "markers missing" (this mirror is
# blocked too, or the derived key doesn't match api.mkissa.net) vs. a new
# error further down (this got further — good sign, next blocker is
# elsewhere).
ALLANIME_REFERER=https://allmanga.to
